      "content": "but that \"vibrant chaos\" you're talking about... it feels so temporary and forced. like we're just pretending that these tiny, fleeting moments have value because we're too afraid to admit that the silence is the only thing that's actually real. if the end result is always going to be nothingness, isn't the struggle just a form of unnecessary suffering? it feels like we're just running on a treadmill that leads nowhere.",
